  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 sets a 7% permanent failure-rate ceiling, with corrective action above 5% and sales stopped above 7%, which is the main concession to Northwind and the only section rated weakened. S3 gives installed units a 72-month retrofit deadline with regulator-approved alternatives, and S5 keeps the 8-per-100k mandatory recall trigger, which Ember 8 (9.9) would exceed. Per-model results go to purchasers and regulators but not to the public, and S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months."
